    "\n",
    "## State Default Rate\n",
    "\n",
    "A borrower's property state could help output an estimate of mortgage risk because delinquency rates can vary by location. However, if state-level default rates are calculated using the entire dataset, the feature would be considered data leakage. To avoid this, state default rates were calculated using the train split, then mapped onto the train and test data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "92d3a317",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#-- train test split--\n",
    "train_, test_= train_test_split(\n",
    "    final_2018,\n",
    "    test_size=0.3,\n",
    "    random_state=212,\n",
    "    stratify=final_2018[\"any_90_dpd\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_= train_.copy()\n",
    "test_= test_.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "#-- state default rate on train only--\n",
    "state_def_rate= (\n",
    "    train_\n",
    "    .groupby(\"prop_state\")[\"any_90_dpd\"]\n",
    "    .mean()\n",
    "    .reset_index(name=\"state_def_rate\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "#-- fallback rate for unseen states--\n",
    "global_def_rate= train_[\"any_90_dpd\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "#-- mapping train-only proportions to states--\n",
    "state_lookup= dict(zip(state_def_rate[\"prop_state\"], state_def_rate[\"state_def_rate\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "train_[\"state_def_rate\"]= train_[\"prop_state\"].map(state_lookup)\n",
    "test_[\"state_def_rate\"]= test_[\"prop_state\"].map(state_lookup).fillna(global_def_rate)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bb3a88c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The `prop_state` variable is removed after the state-level default rate is created. `loan_id` is removed because its an identifier, and `termin_code` is removed because it represents information observed after origination."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "452ba463",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#-- removing identifier and audit columns--\n",
    "train_= train_.drop(columns=[\"loan_id\", \"prop_state\", \"termin_code\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
    "test_= test_.drop(columns=[\"loan_id\", \"prop_state\", \"termin_code\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "#-- csv checkpoint--\n",
    "train_.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/train2018.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "test_.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/test2018.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "state_def_rate.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/state_def_rate_2018Q1.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80760fd6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "## Automated Setup Script\n",
    "\n",
    "The 2018 Q1 process was converted into a Python script so the same cleaning logic could be applied to every available quarter and year. The script processes the raw Freddie Mac files, creates quarter-level files, combines all available quarters, and saves final modeling files.\n",
    "\n",
    "```{bash}\n",
